Changelog: 05-11-2026 13:47:39

Added. Upscale Boost: the BC250 Bazzite Suite's BC-250 Upscaler Manager on the Windows handheld, feature for feature,
on the suite's portable window (five cards, every action a controller button in the legend, a second press where the
BC250 app asked in a dialog). HelixSR: Get HelixSR downloads the newest HelixSR 2.x release (checked against the
SHA-256 GitHub publishes), downloads at the same time what its helixsr-setup.ps1 pins (NVIDIA's DLSS DLL, the
embeddable Python with numpy, Microsoft's shader compiler, each checked), runs HelixSR's own builder natively without
frame generation and without its game installer, and keeps the result as the payload; Cancel, Check now (also at
start, which the More tab turns off), the fallback HelixSR 1.8.1, NVIDIA's DLL from a game found in Steam or picked in
the browser, and Import of a release folder or zip. Games: every Steam game (every library in libraryfolders.vdf) and
any folder added in the browser, looked through off the window's thread for an FSR 3.1 DLL; Run with HelixSR puts
HelixSR in place of the game's DLL (the game's own kept as .original.dll) and starts the game through Steam, never
while it runs; Go back puts the game's DLL back. OptiScaler: HelixSR's stand-alone folder, OptiScaler beside the
game's .exe (from a 1.7.0 to 1.8.1 payload; Windows needs no launch options), a second upscaler, and the OptiScaler.ini
lines copied. Deployments: every place HelixSR was put with its state, Update older games, Go back and Forget.
Settings: helixsr.ini in three tabs, saved as the payload's at once with its comments kept, Defaults, Apply to a game.
Log: where HelixSR is kept, and the app's log read in the app.
